{"title":"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Simple_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Simple Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Similar_to_Solution_1,_1_and_2_combined)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Similar to Solution 1, 1 and 2 combined)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rudolph bikes at a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Constant\" title=\"Constant\">constant</a> rate and stops for a five-minute break at the end of every mile. Jennifer bikes at a constant rate which is three-quarters the rate that Rudolph bikes, but Jennifer takes a five-minute break at the end of every two miles. Jennifer and Rudolph begin biking at the same time and arrive at the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-mile mark at exactly the same time. How many minutes has it taken them?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Simple_Solution\">Simple Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Simple Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the time Rudolph takes disregarding breaks and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/0/9406d161197fe07aa9ee934d5c86671b6d18d8e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{3}r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"21\" height=\"37\" /> be the time Jennifer takes disregarding breaks. We have the equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe61982caf36e5503b1bb01e927c976127d43373.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r+5\\left(49\\right)=\\frac{4}{3}r+5\\left(24\\right)\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/7/b47a7b4a6e55c61bf36af9f998f6249802c643cb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[125=\\frac13r\\]\" width=\"71\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f452edd887b2426bdf31faf1afbd46f6265cc78.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r=375.\\]\" width=\"63\" height=\"12\" />\nThus, the total time they take is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/9/799d1234f5d0bcb574672f96747dcc6696b92076.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$375 + 5(49) = \\boxed{620}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"23\" /> minutes.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let Rudolf bike at a rate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, so Jennifer bikes at the rate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/4/6349943859b3b944f4109855c576a85b519b900e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac 34r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"21\" height=\"38\" />. Let the time both take be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />. \n</p><p>Then Rudolf stops <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/c/34c8e6bf4d57cd6f2bb0d7d43e00f0f442f53b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> times (because the rest after he reaches the finish does not count), losing a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/b/d5b3d899cc0c4f43946f2908b402aeb40d77ac7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49 \\cdot 5 = 245$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> minutes, while Jennifer stops <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times, losing a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/0/ea01e1d9654a5a57bc91caf919faf485844fdf38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24 \\cdot 5 = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"91\" height=\"13\" /> minutes. The time Rudolf and Jennifer actually take biking is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/4/dc4086713913834e37ef3a58e25ab942c1688bdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t - 245,\\, t-120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"122\" height=\"16\" /> respectively. \n</p><p>Using the formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fddee21cdc2ba1767d6462342e519da74b3a9e07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac dt$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" />, since both Jennifer and Rudolf bike <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> miles,\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/009c2785ed941a2e6127ad143e7d0958eeb670b9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align}r &amp;= \\frac{50}{t-245}\\\\ \\frac{3}{4}r &amp;= \\frac{50}{t-120} \\end{align}\" width=\"289\" height=\"82\" /></center>\n<p>Substituting equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> into equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and simplifying, we find \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/3/903cba8139ad0245619f6ae90070a72bf9bb6c06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}50 \\cdot \\frac{3}{4(t-245)} &amp;= 50 \\cdot \\frac{1}{t-120}\\\\ \\frac{1}{3}t &amp;= \\frac{245 \\cdot 4}{3} - 120\\\\ t &amp;= \\boxed{620}\\ \\text{minutes} \\end{align*}\" width=\"240\" height=\"115\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the total time that Jennifer and Rudolph bike, including rests, to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" /> minutes.  Furthermore, let Rudolph's biking rate be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> so Jennifer's biking rate is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/8/8d8cd1671fa03fc060cff105e4742898596ad5c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{4}r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"21\" height=\"38\" />. Note that Rudolf takes 49 breaks, taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/457e0238b37e2800c69f358efc15d6190a2b5a70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49\\cdot 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> minutes, and Jennifer takes 24 breaks, taking <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/4/324f5312c5b01c15e4abfbb0b326764cd9b4bdd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24\\cdot 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> minutes.  Since they both reach the 50 mile mark, then by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1218dbfae7805ea5564ac7ee2a892d0a846653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=rt$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />, the rate times time taken for Rudolph and Jennifer must equal.  Hence, we disregard the breaks from the total time taken and get the equation  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/0/a50c53b8ac32c705276201096447c8e51d85212a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r(t-49\\cdot 5)=\\frac{3}{4}r(t-24\\cdot 5),\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"37\" />yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/c/a3c02d21ea4168a6b30c012d2a35c1cd59e78c0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t=\\boxed{620}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"71\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Similar_to_Solution_1.2C_1_and_2_combined.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Similar_to_Solution_1,_1_and_2_combined)\">Solution 3 (Similar to Solution 1, 1 and 2 combined)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Similar to Solution 1, 1 and 2 combined)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Recall <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1218dbfae7805ea5564ac7ee2a892d0a846653.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=rt$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />. So, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/8/c88c5fe05e5c1d4530aced1ab38fe9867f136298.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d = r(t-(49\\cdot 5))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the speed of Rudolph, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e0c7d8816ce487cdad503069a42dbbdcf779c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\frac{3}{4}r(t-(24 \\cdot 5))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"155\" height=\"38\" />, describing Jennifer analogously. We amalgamate the two equations and reduce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a5316be9a5fbcb517e1a96b09a84b948a26d0ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t-245 = \\frac{3}{4}t - 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"142\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/f/a9f052e3f207fdc2800dc3d830e1b3e68f430114.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}t = 155$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b860250d959301362a84a22c552f2d940b84137c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t = \\boxed{620}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"71\" height=\"25\" />. Here, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is unimportant, saving time, just like the simple solution stated previously.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II\" title=\"2008 AIME II\">2008 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2008 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2008\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2008 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017214447\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.053 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.085 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 281/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1806/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6945/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   15.129      1 -total\n 60.82%    9.201      1 Template:AIME_box\n 36.78%    5.564      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6665:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017214447 and revision id 284748. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}